id: pm-eqlsg9
title: "Item transaction compensation has two fail-open or fail-stuck edges: an item write that landed without its history event, and a format upgrade that restore retains"
description: "Reported by the second Codex review of PR 1764; both predate the finalize row and affect update rows the same way. (1) The item store replaces the item file and then appends the history event. A process that stops between the two leaves a changed item whose history is unchanged. On resume a step with a match guard judges the already-changed value, refuses, and compensation finds history equal to its captured prefix, so it returns without restoring; the coordinator then treats the step as compensated while the unjournaled change stays on disk. (2) A step that raises pm_format_version (for example by writing deferred_fields on an older item) is restored with the newer format stamp retained, so the restored document hash differs from the sibling step's recorded after_hash and hasOwnedCompensationEffects refuses the sibling with transaction_partial_mutation although no other writer touched the item. The second edge fails closed; the first leaves an unowned change."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[4]: "area:sdk",compensation,durability,transactions
created_at: "2026-11-21T20:55:26.247Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-21T20:55:26.247Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: "Compensation and resume detect an item whose document hash differs from the after_hash of its newest history entry and refuse with a typed error that names the item and the divergence, instead of reporting the step compensated; A fault-injection spec stops the store between the item write and the history append for an update row and a finalize row with a match guard; A batch whose later step raised the item format compensates every step when no other writer intervened, or refuses the format-raising step before it writes, proven by a spec on a format-1 item; The ownership hash fence is not weakened"
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: medium
confidence: medium
expected_result: "A crash between the item write and its history event is detected on recovery, and a format upgrade inside a batch does not block the batch's own rollback"
actual_result: "The unjournaled change survives a reported compensation, and a format upgrade makes the sibling step refuse with transaction_partial_mutation"
